<title>USA: Wandel &amp; Goltermann named chairman.</title>
<headline>Wandel &amp; Goltermann named chairman.</headline>
<dateline>RESEARCH TRIANGLE PARK, N.C. 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wandel &amp; Goltermann Technologies Inc said Thursday that Albrecht Wandel was elected its board chairman, replacing Herbert Bayer who is retiring.</p>
<p>Joachim Simmross was elected to fill the seat vacated by Bayer, the company said.</p>
<p>Bayer, 62, had served as a director of the company since 1986 and as chairman July 1995, the company said.</p>
<p>Wandel, 52, is a co-founder of Wandel &amp; Goltermann Technologies as well as president and chief executive officer of Wandel &amp; Goltermann Management Holding GmbH.</p>
<p>Simmross, 55, served most recently as director of Hannover Finanz GmbH and has served as a member of the Advisory Board of Wandel &amp; Goltermann Group since 1995.</p>
